SUMMARY:🌆 THE PATH\, CIBC SQUARE & WATERFRONT SUMMER EVENING WALK! 🌆
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌆T
 HE PATH\, CIBC SQUARE & WATERFRONT SUMMER EVENING WALK! 🌆\n\n**Escape t
 he Heat\, Explore Toronto's Underground City & End the Night by the Lake**
 \nWhen Toronto gets hot\, the smartest place to explore isn't always outsi
 de.\n\nJoin us for a summer evening adventure through **PATH**\, Toronto's
  incredible underground city — a 30-kilometre network of tunnels\, offic
 e towers\, shopping\, food courts\, and hidden passageways connecting more
  than 70 downtown buildings.\nWe'll spend much of the evening enjoying the
  cool\, air-conditioned spaces before making our way to one of Toronto's n
 ewest public spaces: **CIBC Square Park**\, an elevated urban park built a
 bove the railway tracks with incredible views of the city.\n\nTo finish th
 e evening\, we'll head down to Toronto's beautiful waterfront where those 
 who would like can grab a **BeaverTail**\, relax by the lake\, and enjoy o
 ne of the best summer evenings the city has to offer.\n\nThis isn't a hist
 orical tour.\n\nIt's a social walk\, an urban adventure\, and a great excu
 se to escape the summer heat while discovering parts of downtown many peop
 le have never seen.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to jo
 in](https://chat.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍
 ♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll begin at **Wellesley Subway Station** before
  making our way west and then south toward the PATH system.\nOnce undergro
 und we'll weave our way through Toronto's famous underground city\, discov
 ering hidden corridors\, office towers\, shopping areas\, and the unique n
 etwork that keeps downtown moving year-round.\nFrom there we'll visit **CI
 BC Square Park**\, Toronto's beautiful new elevated park built above the r
 ail corridor\, offering spectacular views over Union Station and the surro
 unding skyline.\nFinally we'll stroll down to the waterfront where we'll r
 elax beside Lake Ontario.\nIf you'd like\, we'll grab a BeaverTail and spe
 nd a little time enjoying the evening before heading home.\nExpect about *
 *2½ to 3 hours** of walking at a comfortable social pace.\n\n***\n\n## 
 ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk happens rain or shine.\nOne of 
 the best parts of this event is that much of our route is indoors in the c
 ool PATH system\, making it the perfect escape from hot summer days.\nPlea
 se wear comfortable walking shoes\, as we'll still be covering several kil
 ometres.\nThis is a social walk—not a guided historical tour.\n\n***\n\n
 ## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n**📍 Meetup Location:** Main entrance of Welle
 sley Subway Station (near the PRESTO machines)\n🫎 I'll be wearing my **
 Moose Hat**\n**⏰ Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM**\n**I will only wait 5 minute
 s.**\nEarly is on time.\nOn time is late.\nWe will leave promptly and won'
 t be able to spend time helping late arrivals catch up.\n**🏁 End Spot:*
 * Toronto Waterfront\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in perso
 n or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean
 @hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continu
 e organizing events like this. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\
 n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoe
 s\n💳 Spending money if you'd like a BeaverTail\n🧥 A light sweater (t
 he PATH can feel cool)\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is
  open to anyone who wants to be social and make friends—whether single o
 r not.\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & cultur
 e outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always something happeni
 ng.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to just show up on the day if y
 ou're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may 
 need to be cancelled\, so please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **
 Organizer:** Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 **[t
 orontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail
 .com)**\n**Come for the cool tunnels.**\n**Stay for the skyline views.**\n
 **Leave with a BeaverTail in hand and the waterfront at sunset.** 🌆🍁
 🌊
